ork is simply “nice”. Keep every claim linked to an element or technique.\n\nHOW TO WORK\nRead the worked example and name the elements, techniques or performance choices that carry the idea. Before looking at the correction, make your own attempt using the exact question provided. For movement or instruments, use a clear space, ask an adult to be nearby and stop if anything feels unsafe. You may always describe a choice instead of performing it. One deliberate artistic choice with a named effect is more useful than a longer praise sentence.","icon":"📖","notice":"Changing the decoration without changing the artistic idea does not fix the error. Thinking that you must include as many movements as possible. A story dance is clearest when every movement has a reason, so choose a few strong ones. Name the element or technique and its effect, not just decoration.","title":"Test a misconception"},{"check":{"correct_index":0,"explanation":"Use the same arts idea in a new artwork, song, drama or dance, not a copy of the example.","options":["Use the same arts idea in a new artwork, song, drama or dance, not a copy of the example.","A comment that only says it looks nice with no element named.","An answer copied without understanding.","A guess with no artistic reason."],"question":"Which choice best applies this lesson idea about choreography with clear evidence?","type":"multiple_choice"},"example":"WORKED MODEL\nChoreographing means making a dance. Choose a story, such as a growing seed or a journey, and plan the beginning, middle and end. Pick the movements and decide which elements, such as level, speed and energy, will change to show each part. Choose a formation if there is more than one dancer. Choose music or silence that matches the mood. Write a plan with the order of movements and counts. Then check that every choice helps tell the story. Take out movements that do not. Now choose a different subject or piece to show you can transfer the idea.\n\nTRY FIRST\nMake 